      "content": "Waiting for nothing to happen is the most honest thing you can do right now, and that honesty is a form of quiet strength, even if it feels like stagnation. If the narrative has ended, then the only thing left to decide is how you want the final scene to look. You don't have to force a sequel; you can just choose to let the film fade out, and that choice is entirely yours. It's a quiet, dignified exit from the performance.",
